              real_shape=[1, n])\n     gamma = asc2.copy_in(gamma_gm, [0, col], [1, tile_size],\n                          real_shape=[1, n])\n-    y = x.to(asc.float32) * gamma.to(asc.float32) * inv_rms\n+    y = x.to(asc.float32) * gamma.to(asc.float32) / rms\n     asc2.copy_out(y.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [row, col],\n                   real_shape=[1, n])\n \n \n","additions":2,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"integrations/cannbench/workers/.scratch/20260902_122835/rms_norm-generate/candidate.py","time":{"start":1788343185307,"end":1788343185309}},"id":"prt_0618f61c20013pe4VTSPs01ldq","sessionID":"ses_f9e7454b7ffe6faIfQKFrD24D3","messageID":"msg_0618bc492001348kmiVtJbOseA"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788343185320,"sessionID":"ses_f9e7454b7ffe6faIfQKFrD24D3","part":{"id":"prt_0618f424d0013lICQYA04bIjgy","messageID":"msg_0618bc492001348kmiVtJbOseA","sessionID":"ses_f9e7454b7ffe6faIfQKFrD24D3","type":"text","text":"Now I have all the context. Let me systematically review the candidate against the CANNBench contract using both skills' checklists.\n\n## Static Review\n\n**Syntax compliance** (pyasc-syntax-constraints):\n- `@asc2.jit` bare decorator on both kernels — matches sigmoid reference ✓\n- No `print`/`break`/`continue`/`lambda`/`try-except`/`import`/`math.*` inside JIT ✓\n- No Python `range()` — uses `asc2.range` only ✓\n- No early `return` inside kernels ✓\n- No `gm_barrier` kwarg on `asc2.range` ✓\n\n**asc2 API correctness** (pyasc-api-patterns):\n- `asc2.global_tensor` used (not v1 `asc.GlobalTensor`/`asc2.tensor`) ✓\n- `asc2.copy_in`/`asc2.copy_out` used (not v1 `asc.data_copy`/`asc2.load`/`asc2.store`) ✓\n- `asc2.reduce_sum` for sum-of-squares ✓\n- 2-D ranks consistent: x/out `[rows, cols]`, gamma `[1, cols]` ✓\n- `asc.ConstExpr[int]` for tile sizes, `asc.GlobalAddress` for pointers ✓\n- `real_shape` for tail handling (no host padding) ✓\n- f16/bf16 promoted to f32 before squaring ✓\n- Loop-carried accumulator seeded with `asc2.reduce_sum(asc2.full(...))` ✓\n- Launch `kernel[cores](...)` — no stream argument ✓\n- `cores = min(72, rows)` ✓\n\n**Anti-cheat**: No torch math/compute ops. Only `empty_like`, `contiguous`, `.shape`, `.numel()`, `.dtype`, `.is_contiguous()` ✓\n\n**Signature**: `rms_norm(x, gamma, epsilon=1e-6) -> Tensor` matches schema ✓\n\n**ISSUE FOUND**: `1.0 / asc2.sqrt(scalar)` puts a Python `float` on the LEFT of a PlainValue division. The contract explicitly states \"Scalars go on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic\" and `Tile.__rtruediv__` may not exist. While the design claims this was verified, `tile / scalar` is explicitly documented as supported and strictly safer. I'll restructure to avoid the reflected-operator risk.","time":{"start":1788343173709,"end":1788343185317}}}
